From 4f08c4f3ca14fd8785663a5a4d01a05f542e2b2d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sankofa <dev@sankofa.dev>
Date: Mon, 29 Jun 2026 23:22:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] boot hook: parse target=source String manifest + dispatch
 repoint (dispatch-funcreg)

SankofaApplyBootPatch (dart_isolate.cc) now:
- reads _sankofaManifest() as a comma-separated String of "target=source" pairs
  (a String, not a List -> the patch carries no _GrowableList, which a slim AOT
  app tree-shakes out and the interpreter can't resolve)
- transplants each base target <- patch source (mapped names; a top-level source
  fn with a constant-return body has no class -> no Object. ctor, so the patch
  references zero base-SDK callables and loads on any slim AOT app)
- captures the target's code entry before transplant and repoints its
  dispatch-table slots to the SankofaDispatchInterpret trampoline + sets the
  function-half (Dart_SankofaCodeEntryForName / Dart_SankofaRepointDispatchToInterpret)
- records repointed= count in sankofa_boot_result.txt

Proven on iPhone 14 Pro: transplanted=2 repointed=2 verify=render-> PATCH-UI-FIXED,
clean boot, from a downloaded bytecode patch -- no flag, no JIT.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
